"🦉 the reviewers await your reply

🌕 lets respond
   │
   ├─ review.peer 1/2
   │  ├─ slug = architect
   │  ├─ verdict = 1 blocker, 0 nitpicks
   │  ├─ contemplate from
   │  │  └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r001._.given.by_peer.architect.md
   │  └─ articulate into
   │     └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r001._.taken.by_self.architect.md
   │
   ├─ review.peer 2/2
   │  ├─ slug = mechanic
   │  ├─ status = retired from the guard config
   │  ├─ verdict = 2 blockers, 0 nitpicks
   │  ├─ contemplate from
   │  │  └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r002._.given.by_peer.mechanic.md
   │  └─ articulate into
   │     └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r002._.taken.by_self.mechanic.md
   │
   ├─ why a retired reviewer still awaits
   │  └─ it spoke, and was then removed from the guard config. what it said
   │     was never answered, and a debt is keyed to the reviewer rather than
   │     to the artifact, so no edit to the artifact can clear it.
   │
   ├─ what to do — answer the retired reviewer
   │  └─ answer it as you would any other — write the .taken above. it will
   │     not speak again, so your answer is what discharges it.
   │
   └─ contemplate each reviewer, then run all 2 — one per reviewer
      ├─ rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.execute --as contemplated --that architect
      └─ rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.execute --as contemplated --that mechanic"
`;

