exports[`formatRouteGuardReviewPeerContemplatePrompt given: [case5] an UNREADABLE reviewer — the counts are fabricated when: [t0] rendered beside a readable reviewer then: matches snapshot 1`] = `
"🦉 the reviewers await your reply

🌕 lets respond
   │
   ├─ review.peer 1/2
   │  ├─ slug = architect
   │  ├─ verdict = 1 blocker, 0 nitpicks
   │  ├─ contemplate from
   │  │  └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r001._.given.by_peer.architect.md
   │  └─ articulate into
   │     └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r001._.taken.by_self.architect.md
   │
   ├─ review.peer 2/2
   │  ├─ slug = mechanic
   │  ├─ verdict = unreadable — no numeric count found
   │  ├─ contemplate from
   │  │  └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r002._.given.by_peer.mechanic.md
   │  └─ articulate into
   │     └─ .behavior/v2026_01_01.demo/.reviews/peer/1.execute._.review.i001.a1b2c3.r002._.taken.by_self.mechanic.md
   │
   ├─ why an unreadable reviewer gates
   │  └─ its output carried no numeric blocker or nitpick count, so no
   │     verdict was ever seen. an absent verdict is not a clean one — to
   │     score it 0/0 would read as an approval nobody granted, so it gates
   │     instead.
   │
   ├─ what to do — name the malfunction
   │  └─ read its .given above — the reviewer malfunctioned, and the .taken
   │     is where you say so. do not hunt for a blocker in it; there is none
   │     to find.
   │
   └─ contemplate each reviewer, then run all 2 — one per reviewer
      ├─ rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.execute --as contemplated --that architect
      └─ rhx route.stone.set --stone 1.execute --as contemplated --that mechanic"
`;

